      "content": "#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstdint>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, m;\n    if (!(cin >> n >> m)) return 0;\n\n    vector<uint64_t> blockedCells;\n    blockedCells.reserve(static_cast<size_t>(m));\n    for (int c = 0; c < m; ++c) {\n        int row, column;\n        cin >> row >> column;\n        blockedCells.push_back(static_cast<uint64_t>(row) * static_cast<uint64_t>(n) +\n                               static_cast<uint64_t>(column));\n    }\n    sort(blockedCells.begin(), blockedCells.end());\n    blockedCells.erase(unique(blockedCells.begin(), blockedCells.end()), blockedCells.end());\n\n    vector<int> dp(n, 0);\n    dp[0] = 1;\n\n    size_t blockedIndex = 0;\n    uint64_t linearIndex = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j, ++linearIndex) {\n            if (blockedIndex < blockedCells.size() && blockedCells[blockedIndex] == linearIndex) {\n                dp[j] = 0;\n                ++blockedIndex;\n            } else if (j != 0) {\n                int sum = dp[j] + dp[j - 1];\n                if (sum >= MOD) sum -= MOD;\n                dp[j] = sum;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << dp[n - 1] << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "An in-place rolling DP and sorted sparse obstacle indices reduce storage to O(N+M) and eliminate the row-copy pass while preserving the recurrence. The column update has a genuine left-to-right dependency, so it remains scalar rather than being incorrectly marked SIMD.",
